=========================================================================================================
21_generalization_holdout.py — published 80/20 split of the generalization cohort
=========================================================================================================

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] What this step does
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Fits a classical stacking ensemble on Morgan fingerprints and a default D-MPNN on the training
  partition that         MoleculeACE publishes for each target, and scores both on its test
  partition. The base-learner combination is         chosen by cross-validation inside the
  training partition only.
  Each model is scored three times: on the whole test partition, on the compounds its authors
  flagged as belonging         to an activity cliff, and on the rest. The cliff subset is where a
  fingerprint representation is expected to be         weakest, so reporting it separately shows
  whether the overall comparison hides a difference there.
